> crt 2 mod 3, 3 mod 5
the system
  2 mod 3: x = 2
    x = 2 (mod 3)
  3 mod 5: x = 3
    x = 3 (mod 5)
x = 8 (mod 15)
  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)
  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution
> crt 1 mod 4, 2 mod 7
the system
  1 mod 4: x = 1
    x = 1 (mod 4)
  2 mod 7: x = 2
    x = 2 (mod 7)
x = 9 (mod 28)
  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)
  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..27: 1 solution
> crt 2 mod 4, 4 mod 6
the system
  2 mod 4: x = 2
    x = 2 (mod 4)
  4 mod 6: x = 4
    x = 4 (mod 6)
x = 10 (mod 12)
  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)
  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..11: 1 solution
> crt 10 mod 12, 3 mod 18
the system
  10 mod 12: x = 10
    x = 10 (mod 12)
  3 mod 18: x = 3
    x = 3 (mod 18)
no solution: the congruences contradict each other (CRT: the residues differ mod the gcd of the moduli)
  check: brute force over 0..35: 0 solutions
> solve 3x = 1 mod 11
  3x = 1 mod 11: 3x = 1: x = 1 * 3^-1 = 1 * 4 = 4
x = 4 (mod 11)
  check: the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..10: 1 solution
> solve 2x = 4 mod 6
  2x = 4 mod 6: 2x = 4: gcd(2, 6) = 2 divides 4: 1x = 2 mod 3, x = 2 (2 solutions mod 6)
x = 2 (mod 3)
  that is, mod 6: x = 2, 5
  check: the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..2: 1 solution
> solve x^2 = 1 mod 8
  x^2 = 1 mod 8: x^2 = 1: square roots mod 8 (Tonelli-Shanks, Hensel, CRT)
x = 1, 3, 5, 7 (mod 8)
  check: each solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..7: 4 solutions
> solve 6x = 4 mod 8
  6x = 4 mod 8: 6x = 4: gcd(6, 8) = 2 divides 4: 3x = 2 mod 4, x = 2 (2 solutions mod 8)
x = 2 (mod 4)
  that is, mod 8: x = 2, 6
  check: the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..3: 1 solution
